Z||000004||deceler8||08-11-2001||10:13 PM||||This is going to sound wierd, but the other day I had to fill out some kind of survey, and they asked about persons I would most like to meet. And I don't know why "ogre" came to mind...<P>Hey...com'on...this guy is one of the best reasons to belong to this forum...why do I imagine him as having a closet full of Fiero T-shirts and Fiero logos on everything he owns ?<P>Gotta love someone who loves the Dukes.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/deceler8_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||08-12-2001||12:39 AM||||The "closet" is mainly full of parts and tools except for the ECM scaner which is usually by the PC. I'd hate to think what that would do to nice Fiero shirts. (Of which I have none, but I did make a theme to go with one of Cliff's wall papers on the PFF CD. No sounds yet but nice cursors and icons. Some cursors are animated.)<P>I've driven big motors and small ones. For day to day stuff I'll take one that's just big enough to get into traffic without panicing. When you figure the 87 4 cyl is making 130+ FP torque, then multiply that in the TC, you're ramming allot more power into the TH125 than most people think. (For it's size, the 4 cyl makes a hell of allot of torque.)<P>I've driven a 4 speed fiero... It moved right along. In the heavy traffic I regularly have to deal with I'd rather have the auto. My worst mileage, AC mostly on and heavy traffic, I'm getting 25mpg. I've gotten as high as 32 out of it when it's all open road.||||reg||6
